lua-pdfio(3)

# NAME

lua-pdfio - Lua wrapper for the pdfio library

# SYNOPSIS

```
local pdfio = require("lua-pdfio")
```

# DESCRIPTION

*lua-pdfio* is a Lua module that provides an interface to the *pdfio* library for
reading and writing PDF files. Most functions map directly onto their pdfio C
counterparts; see *pdfio*(3) for the underlying semantics.

# MODULE FUNCTIONS

*pdfio.open(filename [, password])*
	Opens an existing PDF file. Returns a *file* object or *nil, err*.

*pdfio.create(filename [, version])*
	Creates a new PDF file. *version* defaults to "1.7". Returns a *file*
	object or *nil, err*.

*pdfio.create_output(callback [, version])*
	Creates a PDF file streamed through a Lua *callback(data)* function,
	called for each chunk of output. Useful for building a PDF entirely
	in memory. Returns a *file* object or *nil, err*.

*pdfio.create_temporary([version])*
	Creates a PDF file backed by a unique temporary file. Returns a
	*file* object and the temporary filename, or *nil, err*.

*pdfio.array_create(pdf)*
	Creates a new PDF array associated with the given *pdf* file.

*pdfio.create_icc_obj_from_file(pdf, filename, num_colors)*,
*pdfio.create_icc_obj_from_data(pdf, data, num_colors)*
	Creates an ICC color profile object from a file or in-memory data.

*pdfio.create_color_from_icc_obj(pdf, icc_obj)*,
*pdfio.create_color_from_standard(pdf, num_colors, cs)*,
*pdfio.create_color_from_palette(pdf, num_colors, colors)*,
*pdfio.create_color_from_matrix(pdf, num_colors, gamma, matrix, white_point)*,
*pdfio.create_color_from_primaries(pdf, num_colors, gamma, wx, wy, rx, ry, gx, gy, bx, by)*
	Create a PDF color space array: ICC-based, standard (*cs* is one of
	*pdfio.CS_ADOBE*, *pdfio.CS_P3_D65*, *pdfio.CS_SRGB*, or
	*pdfio.CS_CGATS001*), indexed palette, calibrated matrix, or
	primaries-based, respectively. *matrix* is a 3x3 table and
	*white_point* a 3-element table for the matrix variant.

All of the functions above are also available as *file:*_name_(...)
methods (dropping the leading *pdf* argument), e.g.
*pdf:create_color_from_standard(3, pdfio.CS_SRGB)*.

# FILE METHODS

*file:close()*
	Closes the PDF file.

*file:get_num_pages()*
	Returns the number of pages in the PDF.

*file:get_page(n)*
	Returns the *obj* for page *n* (0-indexed).

*file:create_page([dict])*
	Creates a new page and returns its *stream*.

*file:find_obj(number)*
	Looks up an existing indirect object by its object number.

*file:copy_obj(src_obj)*
	Copies an object from another *file* into this one, returning the
	new object.

*file:copy_page(src_page)*
	Copies a page object from another *file* into this one.

*file:get_permissions()*
	Returns *permissions, encryption* for an encrypted file.

*file:set_permissions(permissions, encryption, owner_password, user_password)*
	Enables encryption on a file being created, with the given
	permission bits (*pdfio.PERMISSION_PRINT*, *pdfio.PERMISSION_COPY*,
	etc.) and encryption mode (*pdfio.ENCRYPTION_AES_128*, etc.).

*file:dict_create()*
	Creates a new PDF dictionary associated with this file.

*file:create_array_obj(array)*, *file:create_name_obj(name)*,
*file:create_number_obj(num)*, *file:create_string_obj(s)*,
*file:create_obj(dict)*
	Low-level helpers to wrap a value as a standalone indirect object.

*file:create_font_obj_from_base(name)*
	Creates a font object from one of the 14 standard PDF base fonts
	(e.g. "Helvetica", "Courier").

*file:create_font_obj_from_data(data, unicode)*
	Embeds a font from in-memory TrueType/OpenType data, without
	touching the filesystem.

*file:create_image_obj_from_file(filename, interpolate)*
	Creates an image object from a JPEG or PNG file.

*file:create_image_obj_from_data(data, width, height, num_colors,
color_data, alpha, interpolate)*
	Embeds an image from an in-memory raw pixel buffer, without
	touching the filesystem. *data* must be at least
	*width* * *height* * (*num_colors* + (*alpha* and 1 or 0)) bytes.

*file:get_author()*, *file:get_title()*, *file:get_version()*, etc.
	Standard metadata getters.

*file:set_author(v)*, *file:set_title(v)*, *file:set_creator(v)*,
*file:set_subject(v)*, *file:set_keywords(v)*
	Standard metadata setters.

*file:get_language()*, *file:set_language(v)*
	Get/set the document language (*/Lang*).

*file:get_id()*, *file:get_name()*
	Return the trailer *ID* array and the file's name, respectively.

*file:set_creation_date(t)*, *file:set_modification_date(t)*
	Set timestamps (Unix time).

*file:add_output_intent(subtype, condition, cond_id, reg_name, info,
profile)*
	Adds an OutputIntent dictionary to the file catalog.

*file:string_create(s)*
	Interns a string in the file's string pool, returning it unchanged.

# OBJECT METHODS

*obj:get_type()*
	Returns the object type string (e.g., "Page", "Catalog").

*obj:get_subtype()*
	Returns the object's sub-type name (e.g., "Image" for an image
	XObject).

*obj:get_dict()*
	Returns the *dict* associated with the object.

*obj:get_rect(key)*
	Returns a rectangle table (*x1, y1, x2, y2*) for a rectangle-valued
	dictionary key, such as "MediaBox".

*obj:get_number()*, *obj:get_generation()*
	Return the object's number and generation, as used by
	*file:find_obj()*.

*obj:get_length()*
	Returns the length of the object's data stream, if any.

*obj:get_name()*
	Returns the object's name, for Name-type objects.

*obj:get_num_streams()*
	Returns the number of content streams for a page object.

*obj:open_page_stream(n, decode)*
	Opens a page's *n*th content stream for reading.

*obj:open_stream(decode)*
	Opens a non-page object's data stream for reading.

*obj:create_stream([filter])*
	Creates a writable data stream for the object, optionally applying
	a compression *filter* (*pdfio.FILTER_FLATE*, etc.).

*obj:image_get_width()*, *obj:image_get_height()*,
*obj:image_get_bytes_per_line()*
	Return dimensions of an image object.

*obj:text_measure(s, size)*
	Measures the width of string *s* at point *size* when set in this
	font object.

*obj:close()*
	Closes the object (e.g. finishes writing its stream).

# DICTIONARY METHODS

*dict[key]*
	Retrieves a value from the dictionary.

*dict:keys()*
	Returns a table containing all keys in the dictionary.

*dict:iterate_keys(fn)*
	Calls *fn(key)* for each key; stops early if *fn* returns *false*.

*dict:set_number(key, val)*, *dict:set_string(key, val)*, etc.
	Sets values in the dictionary.

*dict:add_font(name, font_obj)*, *dict:add_image(name, image_obj)*,
*dict:add_color_space(name, array)*
	Register a font, image, or color space object as a named page
	resource.

*dict:copy(pdf)*, *dict:clear(key)*
	Copies the dictionary into another file, or removes a key.

# ARRAY METHODS

*array[n]*
	Retrieves the *n*th element (1-indexed).

*#array*
	Returns the number of elements in the array.

*array:append_number(val)*, *array:append_string(val)*,
*array:append_boolean(val)*, *array:append_date(val)*,
*array:append_name(val)*, *array:append_binary(val)*,
*array:append_array(val)*, *array:append_dict(val)*,
*array:append_obj(val)*
	Append a value of the corresponding type to the array.

*array:remove(n)*
	Removes the *n*th element (1-indexed).

*array:copy(pdf)*
	Copies the array into another file, returning the new array.

# STREAM METHODS

*stream:read([amt])*
	Reads data from the stream.

*stream:write(data)*
	Writes data to the stream.

*stream:puts(s)*, *stream:putchar(ch)*
	Write raw, unformatted data to the stream.

*stream:peek([amt])*, *stream:consume(bytes)*
	Look ahead in the stream without advancing, or skip bytes.

*stream:get_token()*
	Reads the next whitespace-delimited PDF content token.

*stream:close()*
	Closes the stream.

*stream:draw_image(name, x, y, w, h)*
	Draws a named image resource at the given position and size.

*stream:text_begin()*, *stream:text_end()*, *stream:text_show(unicode, s)*
	Text drawing functions.

*stream:set_text_font(name, size)*, *stream:set_text_matrix(m)*,
*stream:set_text_word_spacing(spacing)*, *stream:set_text_character_spacing(spacing)*,
*stream:set_text_leading(leading)*, *stream:set_text_rendering_mode(mode)*,
*stream:set_text_rise(rise)*, *stream:set_text_x_scaling(percent)*
	Text state setters.

*stream:text_move_to(tx, ty)*, *stream:text_move_line(tx, ty)*,
*stream:text_new_line()*, *stream:text_next_line()*,
*stream:text_show_justified(unicode, fragments)*,
*stream:text_new_line_show(ws, cs, unicode, s)*
	Additional text positioning and drawing functions.

*stream:path_rect(x, y, w, h)*, *stream:path_move_to(x, y)*,
*stream:path_line_to(x, y)*, *stream:path_curve(x1, y1, x2, y2, x3, y3)*,
*stream:path_curve13(x1, y1, x3, y3)*, *stream:path_curve23(x2, y2, x3, y3)*,
*stream:path_close()*, *stream:path_end()*
	Path construction functions. *path_curve13* omits the second control
	point (coincident with the endpoint); *path_curve23* omits the first
	control point (coincident with the current point).

*stream:stroke()*, *stream:fill(even_odd)*,
*stream:fill_and_stroke(even_odd)*, *stream:clip(even_odd)*
	Path painting functions.

*stream:save()*, *stream:restore()*
	Save/restore the graphics state.

*stream:set_dash_pattern(phase, on, off)*, *stream:set_line_cap(cap)*,
*stream:set_line_join(join)*, *stream:set_line_width(w)*,
*stream:set_miter_limit(limit)*, *stream:set_flatness(f)*
	Line and path style setters.

*stream:set_fill_color_device_gray(g)*, etc., and matching
*set_stroke_color_device_\** variants, plus
*set_fill_color_space(name)* / *set_stroke_color_space(name)*
	Fill and stroke color setters (DeviceGray/DeviceRGB/DeviceCMYK and
	named color spaces).

*stream:matrix_concat(m)*, *stream:matrix_rotate(degrees)*,
*stream:matrix_scale(sx, sy)*, *stream:matrix_translate(tx, ty)*
	Current transformation matrix operations.

*stream:begin_marked(tag [, dict])*, *stream:end_marked()*
	Author tagged (marked) content for accessibility.

# SEE ALSO

*pdfio*(3)

